+---
+title: "click.Duration param type: parsing rules and edge cases"
+author: HarzerHeribert
+date: 2026-10-15
+cost: { minutes: 2, tokens: 35826 }
+touches:
+  - docs/api.md
+  - docs/parameter-types.md
+  - src/click/__init__.py
+  - src/click/types.py
+  - tests/test_types.py
+  - CHANGES.md
+---
+
+## Decided
+- `click.Duration` (src/click/types.py, next to `DateTime`) accepts a `datetime.timedelta` unchanged, or a string that is either all ASCII digits (seconds) or `<int>d<int>h<int>m<int>s` groups, each optional but in that order, at least one present, case-insensitive. Everything else, including non-string values like an `int` default, fails with "{value!r} is not a valid duration.".
+- It is exported from `click/__init__.py` and documented in docs/parameter-types.md (an example section plus the listing) and docs/api.md. The docstring says `versionadded:: 8.6.0` because 8.5.0 is already released.
+
+## Tried and ruled out
+- Using `\d` or plain `re.IGNORECASE` lets non-ASCII input through. `\d` matches full-width digits, which `int()` accepts, and a case-insensitive Unicode "s" matches "ſ" (U+017F). The regex uses `[0-9]` with `re.ASCII | re.IGNORECASE`.
+
+## Watch out
+- `convert` must catch `ValueError` (int() rejects digit strings longer than 4300 characters) and `OverflowError` (timedelta rejects more than 999999999 days) and turn them into the same `self.fail` message. Tests cover "9999999999d" and "1" * 5000.
+- No CHANGES.md entry was added: there is no unreleased section after 8.5.0 yet.
